# This project's entire verification model rests on byte-exact files.
#
# state.json must round-trip exactly as JSON.stringify(obj, null, 2) + "\n",
# and every issue, evidence and handover file is pinned by a recorded SHA-256
# in the supervision ledger. Any line-ending translation on checkout would
# break all of it at once — the round-trip precondition, every recorded
# digest, and every frozen-tree aggregate — and would present as wholesale
# corruption rather than as a line-ending problem.
#
# core.autocrlf is true at the system level on the machine where this
# repository was created, so without this file a fresh clone would convert
# 367 committed files to CRLF.
#
# Therefore: never translate line endings for anything, in either direction.
* -text
